{
  "version": 3,
  "name": "Altec 436C",
  "category": "Dynamics",
  "author": "LiveWDF",
  "description": "Altec drawing 8192-1, 600-ohm output strapping. The push-pull 6BC8 gain stage uses three fitted plate-current regions per half to carry remote cutoff into deep reduction. The 6CG7 line output and negative peak feedback rectifier use fitted tube laws. The input gain represents the ganged attenuator. Transformer equivalents use documented replacement ratios. The bias floor and supply are fixed, and heater, meter and mains circuits are outside the audio model.",
